        "role": "user",
        "content": "Skriv endast Python-kod för topo(nodes, edges). nodes är unika strängar; edges är (u,v) som betyder u före v. Returnera en topologisk ordning där den lexikografiskt minsta tillgängliga noden alltid väljs. Dubbla kanter räknas bara en gång. Alla kantändpunkter finns i nodes. Vid cykel, även självloop, kasta ValueError. Ändra inte argumenten. Använd standardbiblioteket."
      }
    ]
  },
  "started_unix": 1791360454.3805654,
  "wall_s": 72.92162503200234,
  "first_token_s": 13.84015322200139,
  "content": "```python\nimport heapq\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\ndef topo(nodes, edges):\n    # Create a set of nodes for quick lookup\n    node_set = set(nodes)\n    \n    # Build adjacency list and in-degree count, handling duplicate edges\n    adj = defaultdict(set)\n    in_degree = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\n    \n    # Process edges, ignoring duplicates\n    seen_edges = set()\n    for u, v in edges:\n        if (u, v) in seen_edges:\n            continue\n        seen_edges.add((u, v))\n        \n        # Check for self-loop\n        if u == v:\n            raise ValueError(\"Cycle detected: self-loop\")\n        \n        adj[u].add(v)\n        in_degree[v] += 1\n    \n    # Initialize min-heap with nodes that have in-degree 0\n    heap = []\n    for node in nodes:\n        if in_degree[node] == 0:\n            heapq.heappush(heap, node)\n    \n    result = []\n    while heap:\n        # Always pick the lexicographically smallest available node\n        node = heapq.heappop(heap)\n        result.append(node)\n        \n        for neighbor in adj[node]:\n            in_degree[neighbor] -= 1\n            if in_degree[neighbor] == 0:\n                heapq.heappush(heap, neighbor)\n    \n    # If not all nodes are in result, there's a cycle\n    if len(result) != len(nodes):\n        raise ValueError(\"Cycle detected\")\n    \n    return result\n```",
